[version]
1.3.4
[date]
2026-10-21
[whatsnew]
- FIXED: CraftOS now boots properly from bootloader menu!
  - Old approach (os.run _G) caused "loop in gettable" in require()
    because ArchOS-CC had polluted _G with Kernel/Process/Scheduler
  - New approach: craftos-shim creates a marker file and reboots.
    On next boot, startup.lua sees the marker and runs vanilla
    CraftOS shell directly with a clean _G (CC:Tweaked reboots
    the whole Lua state).
  - When user types 'exit' in vanilla shell, computer reboots
    normally back into ArchOS-CC.
  - Marker file is one-shot: it's deleted on use, so next boot
    after exiting vanilla shell returns to ArchOS-CC.
[/whatsnew]
[files]
startup.lua
kernel/craftos-shim.lua
latest_update.upd
[/files]
